---
import LayoutV2 from '../layouts/LayoutV2.astro';
---

<LayoutV2
  title="Pricing and licensing · Vibecrafted"
  description="How Vibecrafted's Business Source License 1.1 works, which uses are granted, and how to discuss commercial terms."
  lang="en"
  hasHero={false}
>
  <article class="pricing-page">
    <header class="pricing-page__hero">
      <p class="pricing-page__eyebrow">Pricing · licensing</p>
      <h1>Clear license terms before commercial pricing.</h1>
      <p class="pricing-page__lead">
        Vibecrafted is distributed under the Business Source License 1.1 with
        an Additional Use Grant. Public price tiers have not been announced.
        The repository license is the source of truth for what you can use
        today and when you need a separate commercial arrangement.
      </p>
      <div class="pricing-page__actions">
        <a class="pricing-page__action pricing-page__action--primary" href="mailto:hello@vetcoders.io?subject=Vibecrafted%20commercial%20licensing">
          Discuss commercial terms
        </a>
        <a class="pricing-page__action" href="https://github.com/vetcoders/vibecrafted/blob/main/LICENSE">
          Read the exact license
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="pricing-page__grid" aria-label="Licensing paths">
      <article>
        <p class="pricing-page__kicker">Granted use</p>
        <h2>Use Vibecrafted under BSL 1.1</h2>
        <p>
          Non-production use is covered by BSL 1.1. The Additional Use Grant
          also permits internal production use, and production use by
          individual developers and teams of fewer than five people, provided
          the use is not a competitive offering as defined by the license.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <p class="pricing-page__kicker">Commercial arrangement</p>
        <h2>Contact us for excluded uses</h2>
        <p>
          If your intended use falls outside the current grant, the license
          requires a commercial license or that you refrain from that use.
          Tell us your team size, deployment model, and intended offering so
          we can discuss terms for that specific use.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-page__boundary" aria-labelledby="competitive-boundary">
      <p class="pricing-page__kicker">The boundary</p>
      <h2 id="competitive-boundary">Competitive hosted or embedded offerings</h2>
      <p>
        The Additional Use Grant excludes offering the Licensed Work to third
        parties on a hosted or embedded basis in order to compete with
        Vetcoders' paid versions. The exact definitions and exceptions are in
        the LICENSE file; this page is a plain-language route into that
        contract, not a substitute for it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="pricing-page__closing">
      <h2>Not sure which path fits?</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:hello@vetcoders.io?subject=Vibecrafted%20licensing%20question">hello@vetcoders.io</a>
        with the use you have in mind. Public pricing is not yet published;
        commercial terms are discussed directly.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</LayoutV2>

<style>
  .pricing-page {
    width: min(100% - clamp(2rem, 8vw, 8rem), 74rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 9rem) 0 clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark);
  }

  .pricing-page__hero {
    max-width: 58rem;
  }

  .pricing-page__eyebrow,
  .pricing-page__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pricing-page h1,
  .pricing-page h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .pricing-page h1 {
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.4rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .pricing-page h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.55rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .pricing-page p {
    color: var(--fg-on-dark-dim);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .pricing-page__lead {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
  }

  .pricing-page__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .pricing-page__action {
    padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-dark);
    color: var(--fg-on-dark);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .pricing-page__action--primary {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .pricing-page__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .pricing-page__grid article,
  .pricing-page__boundary {
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-dark);
    background: rgba(var(--v2-paper-rgb), 0.025);
  }

  .pricing-page__boundary {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    border-left-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .pricing-page__grid p,
  .pricing-page__boundary p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .pricing-page__closing {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
  }

  .pricing-page__closing a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .pricing-page__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
